/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - An inverter changes direct current (DC) into alternating current (AC).
   - Older rotary inverters used a DC motor driving an AC generator.
   - A TRU changes 115 V line-to-neutral, 400 Hz AC into 28 V DC.
   - Aircraft AC voltage is quoted line-to-neutral.
   - Pdc is DC output power in W; Vdc is DC voltage in V; Idc is DC current in A; Pac is AC input power in W; η is efficiency as a decimal; Iline is line current in A; VLL is line-to-line AC voltage in V; for a 115 V aircraft AC system, VLL = 11
   - An auto-transformer is one winding with a tap.
   - A current transformer (CT) senses load current.
*/
