/* book Worked example: Q: A transformer rectifier unit is rated 200 A at 28 V DC and is 92 % efficient. It is fed from a 200 V line-to-line (115 V line-to-neutral) three-phase AC bus at unity power factor. Find the DC output power, the AC input power and the line current drawn.
   1. DC output power: Pdc = 28 V × 200 A = 5600 W.
   2. AC input power: Pac = Pdc / η = 5600 / 0.92 = 6086.96 W, about 6090 W.
   3. Line current: Iline = Pac / (√3 × 200 × 1) = 6086.96 / 346.41 = 17.57 A, about 17.6 A.
   Answer: The TRU delivers 5600 W, draws about 6090 W from the AC bus, and takes about 17.6 A per line. */
