/* book exam traps: Do not assume a 24 V NiCd battery has 12 cells; it has 19 or 20 cells. | Do not take a specific-gravity reading just after topping up with water; the acid is diluted until mixing. | Do not read 40 Ah as a continuous 40 A rating; it is 40 A for 1 hour at the 1-hour rate. | Do not call every NiCd capacity loss memory effect; ageing, dry-out and overcharge also reduce capacity, which is why a timed capacity check is used. | Do not use open-circuit voltage alone for NiCd state of charge; its curve is flat. */
